## Kotlin code style

- Always specify type of variables except explicit constructor use:

```kotlin
val someObject: SomeObject /* class specification is required */ = getSomeObject(someArg)
var someNewObject /* class specification is not required, constructor used */ = SomeObject()
```

- If more than one argument is used, each argument should be on a separate line:

```kotlin
fun getSomeObject(
    someArg1: String,
    someArg2: Int
): SomeObject
 ```

- Always specify argument names when calling functions:

```kotlin
val someObject: SomeObject = getSomeObject(
    someArg1 = "someValue1",
    someArg2 = 1
)
```

- Always make 1 separate line after class definition;
- Use comments (including Javadoc comments) only if it realy needed:

```kotlin
interface SomeObjectRepository {

    fun get(id: UUID): SomeObject
    fun save(someObject: SomeObject)
    fun delete(id: UUID)
}
```
\- does not need any comments since naming is obvious
